# Copy to `.env` next to docker-compose.yml and edit. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# The public hostname of this server. Its DNS A record must point at this host before the
# first `docker compose up`, and ports 80 and 443 must be reachable from the internet:
# Caddy obtains the certificate for it automatically. IPv4 only — do NOT publish an AAAA
# record (docs/SERVER-GUIDE.md Part 2 §2: IPv6 clients would all share one address).
LOOM_DOMAIN=loom.example.com

# Backups (DESIGN.md D18, docs/SERVER-GUIDE.md Part 2 §8). The values shown are the
# defaults; uncomment a line to change one.
#
# How often the `backup` service copies the database: a `sleep` duration (30m, 6h, 1d).
# It bounds what a restore from this host can lose.
# LOOM_BACKUP_INTERVAL=6h
# How many copies the backups volume keeps. At 6h, 56 copies reach back 14 days (D8); longer
# history is the off-host copy's job.
# LOOM_BACKUP_KEEP=56
#
# The volume the database lives on. Unset means `loom_loom_data`. deploy/compose/restore.sh
# writes this line when it puts the server on a restored volume; deleting the line goes back
# to the original volume, which a restore leaves as it was.
# LOOM_DATA_VOLUME=
